        "original_id": "71643ae2-e8a7-5a17-94d6-c51ed3e5cde0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beatrice Willard, Richard Nixon, Gerald Ford\n- Organizations: Council on Environmental Quality, U.S. presidency\n- Roles: Adviser, President of the United States, Vice President of the United States, U.S. Representative, U.S. Senator\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Nixon was born on January 9, 1913, and died on April 22, 1994.\n- Richard Nixon served as a U.S. Representative and later as a U.S. Senator from California before becoming vice president.\n- Richard Nixon served as the 36th Vice President of the United States from 1953 to 1961.\n- Richard Nixon served as the 37th President of the United States from 1969 until 1974.\n- Richard Nixon was the only U.S. president to resign from office.\n- In her later years, Beatrice Willard advised U.S. Presidents Richard Nixon and Gerald Ford.\n- Beatrice Willard was the first woman on the Council on Environmental Quality.",
